# =============================================================================
# prologue.dlg  -  Dinner with Dad, then the dare at the Ruffleberg place
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Format: systems/dialogue/dialogue_script.gd (header). Speakers are
# data/characters/<ID>.tres; {kid} and {dog} are the names the player picked;
# the kid is a boy or a girl, so lines about the kid use {he}, {son}, {boy|girl}...;
# any other {key} comes from data/names.json (proper nouns live there).
# Scene commands handled by realms/podunk/ruffleberg_lot.gd:
#   @time <morning|day|golden|night> [seconds]     @end_slice
# Story: docs/design-bible.md sections 4 and 5. Lines here are first drafts.
#
# Written with help from Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code.
# Made with love from your friendly hacker - er2oneousbit
# =============================================================================

== dinner
: {town}. A Tuesday in late October.
DAD: So I said to the guy, "Sir, that's not a lawnmower. That's a lifestyle."
KID: Dad.
DAD: {movie_lawnmower}? The sequel? Nobody?
KID: Nobody, Dad.
: Under the table, {dog} is pretending not to beg. Badly.
DAD: Mom's on nights all week, so it's us and the leftovers. And him.
KID: You still haven't said his name once.
DAD: I'm getting there.
KID: Dex says the Ruffleberg place has a basement that goes down, like, forever.
: Dad's fork stops halfway to his mouth.
DAD (serious): Stay away from that house.
* Why? -> dinner_why
* Okay, okay. -> dinner_okay

== dinner_why
KID: Why? It's just an old house.
DAD: Because I said so.
KID: That's not a reason. That's, like, a {streamer} take.
DAD: It's the only one you're getting. Eat your peas.
-> dinner_end

== dinner_okay
KID: Okay, okay. Relax.
DAD: I'm relaxed.
: He is not relaxed.
-> dinner_end

== dinner_end
@set prologue.dad_warned
: Dad doesn't say much for the rest of dinner.
: Later, the house is quiet. {dog} is already asleep across the foot of the bed.
: {kid}'s phone buzzes. Maya: "they're doing it. ruffleberg place. 9. you coming???"

== lot_arrive
: The Ruffleberg place. Nobody has lived there since before anybody's parents were born.
: Everybody in {town} has dared somebody. Nobody has ever gone in.
KID: ({dog} followed me the whole way. Of course he did.)

== maya
[prologue.talked_to_maya] -> maya_again
MAYA: You actually came.
KID: You texted me with three question marks. That's basically a summons.
MAYA: I texted you so you'd talk Dex out of it. Not so you'd do it.
MAYA: He did this to Jordan last year. Jordan cried. On a livestream.
* "I'm not gonna cry." -> maya_brave
* "I just came to watch." -> maya_watch
* [prologue.dad_warned] "My dad told me to stay away." -> maya_dad

== maya_brave
KID: I'm not gonna cry.
MAYA: Everybody says that. Then a raccoon happens.
-> maya_end

== maya_watch
KID: I just came to watch.
MAYA (relieved): Good. Watching is good. Watching is free.
-> maya_end

== maya_dad
KID: My dad told me to stay away from this place. Like, specifically.
MAYA: Your dad? Your dad is the least dramatic person in {town}.
KID: That's what's weird about it.
-> maya_end

== maya_end
@set prologue.talked_to_maya
MAYA: Whatever happens, I'll be right here by the fence. Text me.

== maya_again
[!prologue.dared] MAYA: Dex is waiting. You don't have to give him anything, you know.
[prologue.dared] MAYA: If you're not back in an hour, I'm calling somebody.
[prologue.dared] KID: Who?
[prologue.dared] MAYA: I don't know! Somebody with a flashlight bigger than a phone.

== dex
[prologue.dared] -> dex_again
DEX: Look who showed up. And {he} brought a dog. Cute.
KID: He followed me. He does that.
DEX: Here's the deal. You go in, you go down to the basement, you bring something back.
DEX: Anything. A spoon. A creepy doll. A ghost, if it fits in your pocket.
DEX: Or you're a baby forever. Like, legally.
* "Easy." -> dex_easy
* "What do I get?" -> dex_what
* [prologue.talked_to_maya] "Maya says it's a bad idea." -> dex_maya

== dex_easy
KID: Easy. I've done scarier drops in {game_battle_royale}.
DEX: That's a video game, {man|girl}.
KID: Ranked is scarier than a house.
-> dex_end

== dex_what
KID: What do I get?
DEX: You get to not be a baby forever. That's a pretty big deal.
-> dex_end

== dex_maya
KID: Maya says it's a bad idea.
DEX: Maya says everything is a bad idea. Maya says cereal is a bad idea after nine.
MAYA: It IS a bad idea after nine!
-> dex_end

== dex_end
@set prologue.dared
DEX: Gate's that way. Clock's ticking.
@time night 4
: The last of the sun slides down behind the trees.

== dex_again
DEX: Gate's that way, baby. I mean, {buddy|girl}.

== gate
[!prologue.dared] -> gate_not_yet
: The gate isn't locked. It just looks like it should be.
KID: ({dog}, go home. Seriously.)
: {dog} sits down on {kid}'s foot and stays there.
KID: (Okay. Together, then.)
@end_slice

== gate_not_yet
KID: (Not yet. Dex is going to make a whole thing out of this either way.)
